{
  "root_cause": "When the focused element inside the basket dialog is removed, the focus trap's mutation observer attempts to restore focus to the initial focus node. However, the initial focus node may not be focusable (e.g., if it is disabled or hidden), causing the focus to escape to the body. The existing fallback in tryFocus only retries the initial focus node, which may not resolve the issue.",
  "repair_strategy": "Enhance the mutation removal handler to, if the initial focus node is not focusable, attempt to focus the first focusable node found in the trap's containers.",
  "edits": [
    {
      "path": "index.js",
      "sha256": "17ff10072d68a0aabb1e15fdc42b3a1dee1774dc2ced6facc4753e9a5ae89f90",
      "before": "const checkDomRemoval = function (mutations) {
  const isFocusedNodeRemoved = mutations.some(function (mutation) {
    const removedNodes = Array.from(mutation.removedNodes);
    return removedNodes.some(function (node) {
      return node === state.mostRecentlyFocusedNode;
    });
  });

  // If the currently focused is removed then browsers will move focus to the
  // <body> element. If this happens, try to move focus back into the trap.
  if (isFocusedNodeRemoved) {
    tryFocus(getInitialFocusNode());
  }
};",
      "after": "const checkDomRemoval = function (mutations) {
  const isFocusedNodeRemoved = mutations.some(function (mutation) {
    const removedNodes = Array.from(mutation.removedNodes);
    return removedNodes.some(function (node) {
      return node === state.mostRecentlyFocusedNode;
    });
  });

  // If the currently focused is removed then browsers will move focus to the
  // <body> element. If this happens, try to move focus back into the trap.
  if (isFocusedNodeRemoved) {
    let node = getInitialFocusNode();
    if (!node || !node.focus) {
      // Try to get a focusable node from the trap's containers
      for (const container of state.containers) {
        const nodes = focusable(container);
        if (nodes.length > 0) {
          node = nodes[0];
          break;
        }
      }
    }
    if (node && node.focus) {
      tryFocus(node);
    }
  }
};"
    }
  ],
  "expected_accessibility_effect": "Focus will remain trapped within the basket dialog when items are removed, ensuring keyboard users can continue interacting with the dialog without losing context.",
  "functional_risks": [
    "If the initial focus node is not focusable but another node is, focus may shift to an unexpected node within the dialog, which could be disorienting for some users.",
    "If no focusable node is found in the trap's containers (which should not occur given the trap's requirements), focus will not be restored, but this scenario is unlikely.",
    "The added loop over containers and call to focusable may have a minor performance impact, but the number of containers is typically small."
  ],
  "verification_requirements": [
    "After removing an item from the basket, focus must remain within the basket dialog (i.e., #basket:focus-within must be true).",
    - The item count must update correctly (e.g., from '3 items' to '2 items').",
    - The close button and remove buttons for remaining items must remain focusable and operable via keyboard.",
    - Trapping focus should still function correctly for other scenarios (e.g., tabbing within the dialog, escaping with Escape key)."
  ]
}

